.TH x86info 1
.SH NAME
x86info \- display x86 CPU diagnostics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B x86info
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B x86info
displays a range of information about the CPUs present in an x86 system.
.PP
To make full use of it the CPUID and MSR device drivers need to be available,
with accessible device files
.I /dev/cpu/<n>/cpuid
and
.IR /dev/cpu/<n>/msr .
Options marked
.I (root)
need to be run as root.
.SH OPTIONS
Long options start with two dashes.
Only the single letter forms shown below exist; there are no multi-letter
short options.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Show everything.  As a normal user the root-only outputs are skipped, with a
note on stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-addr
Show physical and virtual address sizes.
.TP
.B \-\-all\-cpus
Report every CPU separately, even when they are identical.
.TP
.B \-\-apic
Dump the local APIC registers.
.I (root)
.TP
.B \-\-bios
Show BIOS information.
.I (root)
.TP
.B \-\-bugs
Show known CPU bugs.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cache
Show TLB, cache sizes and cache associativity.
.TP
.B \-\-connector
Show the CPU socket or slot type.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Show extra debugging output.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-flags
Show CPU feature flags.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of options.
.TP
.B \-\-mhz
Measure the TSC rate, which is the CPU clock on older CPUs.  Takes one second
per CPU measured.
.TP
.B \-\-microcode
Show the microcode revision.
.I (root)
.TP
.B \-\-mptable
Dump the MP table showing the CPUs the BIOS knows about.
.I (root)
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-msr
Dump model specific registers.  Only supported on some processors.
.I (root)
.TP
.B \-\-mtrr
Dump the memory type range registers.
.I (root)
.TP
.B \-\-pm
Show power management information.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-raw\-cpuid
Show register values from all possible CPUID calls.
.TP
.B \-\-show\-machine\-check
Show machine check exception information.
.I (root)
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show verbose descriptions.
